nt  and design of clinical trials  the last uh concentration that we came  up with was assay development these are  for our true  entrepreneurs and there's a very  entrepreneurial spirit at kgi  and so for those students who have taken  all this information and have a great  idea for a new product  we wanted them to know what it would  take to bring it to market  and so this puts together some of our  business and science courses  including the food and drug law and our  advanced in vitro diagnostics business  operations  and again some of the fundamental papers  just to understand what is actually  needed in the field  so these are our three concentrations i  will say most of our students so far  have chosen the clinical decision  support pathway  and for those working in precision  medicine i think this  is the pathway that best um  captures the skills knowledge and  expertise  that will be needed to be an effective  precision medicine specialist  now the heart of our program is actually  what happens when the students are off  campus  and that's the summer experience because  i think  nothing helps the students really  understand what all of this didactic  coursework means  than seeing it put into practice so all  of our students complete a summer  internship at either a clinical genomics  lab  a company a research center  below you see the place where our first  cohort spent their summer  so we had students at labcorp by marin  st  jude scripps translational merck and the  nih  and this experience really gave all of  our students  an insight into what skills were really  used day-to-day  and why they needed to know all those  things that i told them that they needed  to know  and we hope that the summer experience  translates into their capstone project  as i said in the second year the  students spend 18 hours a week working  on a project  and if everything goes to plan they will  just extend their  summer internship project however we do  have some places where this is not  possible  or they get really interested in  something else  so it's not a requirement but  we also have these capstone projects  that allow our students to work  at sites like these to do a more  long-term  and in-depth project so i ask all of you  listening if you have  a project that you've always wanted to  work on and  just don't have enough time for it um  think whether one of our students might  be able to help you in either the summer  or in the school year to really make it  into an interesting and useful product  and project and base of knowledge for  the rest of the fields by  having a project for one of our students  so so far i've talked to you about this  program as if it is still taking place  at kgi  um we had our first cohort came on  campus in the fall of 2018  and they were scheduled to graduate  next month unfortunately they are not  going to be able to have their  commencement  in may as it was planned because we have  gone completely online  all of these programs were designed in  person  with the summer internship experience  but you know we always talked about well  what if the  second year was online then they could  work anywhere in the united states they  wouldn't have to work in southern  california  they could maybe telecommute to sites  all over the country and there was a  general feel that  sometime in the future we would put  portions of this  online of course one week  before spring break we were told that we  would not be coming back to campus due  to the coronavirus  and so we had nine days to convert  our entire curriculum to online  education and i will  say that i have been extremely thankful  for the  grace of our students that they have  made it work and our  faculty have made it work and so right  now we are fully online  but i'll put an asterisk because this is  fully online with  a temporary feel to it we're using zoom  we're doing the best we can but it's  still based on what we would have done  in a classro